          "headline": "Revolut breach affects 680 customers; firm says no direct ransom demand was received",
          "summary": "Revolut's investigation identified 680 customers whose information was disclosed after an attacker used a genuine government-agency email account to submit fraudulent information requests that the firm treated as authentic. Exposed data included passport or identity-card details, home addresses, verification images, bank-account information and Bitcoin activity. Revolut says its systems and customer funds were not compromised, it has received no direct contact or ransom demand from those claiming responsibility, and the UK Information Commissioner's Office is investigating.",
